# Alacrium Portable for Linux README

## Copyright (c) 2026 Alex313031

This is a portable build of Alacrium which can also be used to install/use Alacrium on Linux distros that do not use .deb packages. The ALACRIUM-PORTABLE script and ALACRIUM-SHELL script will need to be made executable with `sudo chmod +x`, and when run will disable logging, default browser check, and set the user data dir to .config/alacrium in this folder rather than the usual $HOME/.config/alacrium folder.

The .desktop files are the equivalents, however one needs to make a symlink to them in either ~/.local/share/applications or /usr/share/applications.
You can also copy the desktop files to a standard applications directory and
edit their `Exec=` lines to use the absolute path where the archive was
unpacked. Full paths are required; `~` and `$HOME` are not expanded there.

The same can be done for the Icon lines, so that they point to the correct locations and show an actual icon.
The alacrium_shell.png is for setting the icon for alacrium-shell.desktop

Thanks for using Alacrium and feel free to use the issues or discussions for problems, questions, features, or suggestions.

	- Alex313031
